Subject: TimezoneSelector: size the floating toolbar to its contents and padding

The toolbar under the map set its width to the row's implicit width, so the
row got that width less the toolbar's left and right padding. Its two combo
boxes do not shrink below their implicit width, and the time-zone box ran
past the panel's right edge. Without the width binding the toolbar takes its
implicit width, the row plus its padding. The height keeps its binding. The
location box takes the same right margin the region box has, so the row's
ends are symmetric with and without the location box.

--- a/components/timezoneselector/TimezoneSelector.qml	2026-10-27 17:02:06.000000000 +0530
+++ b/components/timezoneselector/TimezoneSelector.qml	2026-11-23 19:18:06.327264884 +0530
@@ -327,7 +327,6 @@
             anchors.bottomMargin: Kirigami.Units.gridUnit
             anchors.horizontalCenter: parent.horizontalCenter
 
-            width: mainLayout.implicitWidth
             height: mainLayout.implicitHeight + Kirigami.Units.largeSpacing * 2
 
             contentItem: RowLayout {
@@ -381,6 +380,7 @@
 
                 QQC2.ComboBox {
                     id: locationComboBox
+                    Layout.rightMargin: Kirigami.Units.largeSpacing
 
                     visible: regionComboBox.currentText !== regionComboBox.chooseText
                     displayText: currentText
